  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{3}{20}$ on the left and $\\frac{15}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129810/assets/a9d43ba0a45ea09cca23c929380f4c97a7e28ef959f04701236b9696163f26e7.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $3$ shaded pieces, and the shape on the right has $15$ shaded pieces. So, the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $5.$\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{20}\\times 5=\\frac{15}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
